    "notes": "July 2013 exterior of the former ESMA Officers’ Quarters, the building that later became the ESMA Museum and Site of Memory. Includes the avenue entrance, white plaster and exposed brick, clay roofs, three connected arms and the two open rear courts. The wider former naval campus and the 2015 exhibit structures are outside the 2013 scope. Principal porch location and height are approximate because the mapping outline generalizes the avenue façade."
